        ],
        "statement": "Let m,n∈N with m,n≥1 and A∈M_{m×n}(R)=R^{m×n}. Put [m]={1,…,m} and [n]={1,…,n}. The library indexes vector coordinates and matrix columns by n={0,…,n−1} and matrix rows by m={0,…,m−1}; relabel by j↦j−1, writing u_j=u(j−1), A_ij=A(i−1,j−1), and (Au)_i=Σ_{j=1}^n A_ij u_j. Set ker A={h∈R^n:Ah=0}. For h∈R^n and S⊆[n], h_S is h on S and zero elsewhere; S^c is the complement in [n]. Define ||u||_1=Σ_{j=1}^n|u_j|, the library's p=1 norm under this relabeling. For s∈N with 1≤s≤n, A satisfies the strict nullspace property of order s when ||h_S||_1<||h_{S^c}||_1 for every nonzero h∈ker A and every S⊆[n] with |S|≤s. This condition concerns exact kernel vectors only and contains no measurement-residual term.",
