        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let n,d,s∈N with n≥1, d≥2, 1≤s≤d/2, and σ>0. Use one-based coordinates j=1,…,d corresponding to library coordinate j−1. Put Θ_{s,d}={θ∈R^d: at most s coordinates are nonzero} and let I_d be the d×d identity matrix. For θ∈Θ_{s,d}, observe independent Y_j∼N((I_dθ)_j,σ²/n). The zero kernel gives noiseless strict-NSP recovery of each θ; in the noisy model every Borel estimator T:R^d→R^d has worst-case squared-ℓ2 risk at least σ²s log(ed/s)/(200000n).",
